---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
---

<Layout 
  title="Gravitational Lensing Cheat Sheet | Free Strong, Weak, Microlensing"
  description="Complete gravitational lensing cheat sheet with strong, weak, and microlensing. Free download for physics students."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>Gravitational Lensing<br><span>Cheat Sheet</span></h1>
    <p>Strong, weak, and microlensing. From light bending to dark matter detection.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Basic Physics</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Einstein's Prediction</h3>
        <pre><code>Light bends in gravitational field
Deflection angle: α = 4GM/(c²b)
b: impact parameter
First confirmed: Eddington 1919 (solar eclipse)</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Strong Lensing</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Strong Lensing Effects</h3>
        <pre><code>Einstein rings: source directly behind lens
Multiple images: 2, 4, or odd number
Arcs: distorted background galaxies
Einstein radius: θ_E = √(4GM/c² × (d_ls)/(d_l d_s))</code></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Applications</h3>
        <pre><code>Mass measurement of galaxies/clusters
Time delays between images
Hubble constant measurement
Dark matter distribution</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Weak Lensing</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Weak Lensing Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Statistical distortion of background galaxies
Shear: coherent shape distortion
No multiple images
Requires many background galaxies
Maps dark matter distribution</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Microlensing</h2>
    <div class="formula-grid">
      <div class="formula-card">
        <h3>Microlensing Properties</h3>
        <pre><code>Temporary brightening of background star
No image splitting (unresolved)
Timescale: days to months
Used to detect exoplanets
Used to detect MACHOs</code></pre>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Download</h2>
    <p>Print this page or save as PDF for quick reference.</p>
    <p><strong>Tip:</strong> Use Ctrl+P (Cmd+P on Mac) to print or save as PDF.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
